1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:02,032
How did a failed wallpaper become bubble

2
00:00:02,032 --> 00:00:02,732
wrap?

3
00:00:02,972 --> 00:00:04,253
Nobody wanted it on their walls...

4
00:00:04,761 --> 00:00:06,799
and it almost ended up in the trash.

5
00:00:07,156 --> 00:00:09,713
In 1957, two engineers sealed two shower

6
00:00:09,713 --> 00:00:11,463
curtains together, trapping rows of air

7
00:00:11,463 --> 00:00:13,617
bubbles inside, and sold it as fancy

8
00:00:13,617 --> 00:00:14,771
textured wallpaper.

9
00:00:15,087 --> 00:00:16,818
So they tried it as greenhouse insulation.

10
00:00:17,452 --> 00:00:18,269
That flopped too.

11
00:00:18,568 --> 00:00:20,164
Then a computer maker needed to ship its

12
00:00:20,164 --> 00:00:21,972
delicate new machine without a single

13
00:00:21,972 --> 00:00:22,672
crack.

14
00:00:22,944 --> 00:00:23,975
The bubbles took the bumps.

15
00:00:24,252 --> 00:00:26,290
The computers arrived safe, and packing

16
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:27,396
was never the same.

17
00:00:27,714 --> 00:00:28,868
So every pop you hear...

18
00:00:28,868 --> 00:00:30,599
is a wallpaper nobody wanted.
